#36528
The Resting Place of Lord Tarrant~
   The stairs end some thirty feet down in a cavernous chamber, the walls of
which are lined with unlit torches thrust into metal sconces, set at regular
intervals around the perimeter.  In between each sconce hangs a portrait, of
knights of ages past.  Above each portrait hangs a coat of arms of that
knight's house, a mark of respect to the knight and to his house.  Piles of
corroded weapons lie atop moldering clothing below each picture; the remains of
the knight's battle garb, worn so bravely in life and now left to rot in death.
Of their bodies, though, there is no sign.  Only a single coffin can be seen in
the room, placed in the center of the chamber, atop a stone plinth.  It is from
this coffin that the breeze, and the sounds it carries, appears to emanate...
  
~
